# DTF tier manifest: github-release-mirror  (artifact-keeper#3656, #3657, #3658;
# all shipped in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + a two-origin, header-recording upstream
# (upstreams.mock-recorder: one stdlib-python server on :80 and :81 of
# 172.16.<slot>.77 with a shared run-time file table). :80 plays github.com /
# api.github.com, :81 the objects host a release download is redirected to.
# Proxy-cache sidecars are read and aged through a throwaway postgres:16-alpine
# container with --volumes-from the backend (the backend image has no shell).
#
# THE BEHAVIOUR
# #3657  `github`, `mise` and `aqua` Remote formats share the generic handler
#        and the /general route; a release asset
#        <o>/<r>/releases/download/<tag>/<asset> gets a finite seven-day cache
#        lifetime instead of the 300 s mutable default. Generic Remotes are
#        unchanged.
# #3656  A repository's upstream token (upstream-auth bearer) must reach the
#        release host but never the objects host the release host redirects
#        to (github.com -> objects.githubusercontent.com in production).
# #3658  On those formats the GitHub API release-by-tag lookup
#        repos/<o>/<r>/releases/tags/<tag> gets the same seven days;
#        releases/latest keeps the 300 s default.
#
# WHAT CORPUS ALREADY COVERS (artifact-keeper-test #399,
# tests/formats/test-github-mirror.sh, not in DTF): format round-trip, private
# rejection, and a real `mise install --locked` through url_replacements. This
# tier adds the facets that script cannot see: the Authorization header on
# each hop, and the cache lifetimes.
#
# THE PRIMITIVE FOR "15 MINUTES LATER"
# The stamped lifetime is read from the entry's __cache_meta__.json
# (expires_at - cached_at), then cached_at and expires_at are both moved back
# 900 s and the path is requested again. A 300 s entry must revalidate
# upstream; a seven-day entry must not. No sleeping.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED on 1.10.0 (no github/mise/aqua format: create answers 400,
#              every later case 404), GREEN on 1.11.0 and main:
#              #3657 github, mise and aqua Remotes create and read back their
#                    format.
#              #3656 through the github Remote: 200 with the objects host's
#                    exact bytes; the release host saw `Bearer <token>`; the
#                    objects host saw no Authorization header.
#              #3657 github and mise release assets stamped 604800 s; aged
#                    15 minutes, served with no upstream request.
#              #3658 releases/tags/<tag> stamped 604800 s and not revalidated
#                    at 15 minutes; releases/latest stamped 300 s and
#                    revalidated.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images, on a generic Remote with the same
#              upstream and token: the token reaches the release host and not
#              the objects host (reqwest strips it cross-origin; #3656 pinned
#              this, it never regressed), and a release asset keeps 300 s and
#              revalidates at 15 minutes.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~30 authenticated calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock is on a private subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-recorder"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
